add('S73','qa_notes','Q4 no explainer comparison; Q6 small case study; Q8 repository link present in p.5 footnote 9, access/completeness not verified; Q10 5 repetitions.','Local N708.txt p.5 footnote 9 and p.6 sampling methodology.')
add('S67','evaluation','Mean pairwise top-10 feature-set overlap across 100 LIME explanations of evaluation instances per model and experimental repetition; reported across 30 repeated holdout evaluations alongside the other trustworthiness dimensions.','Publisher Experimental methodology → Explanation stability defines overlap |Fi∩Fj|/10 and averages all pairs of 100 evaluation-instance explanations.')
add('S67','qa_notes','Q5 separate top-10 LIME feature-overlap measure; comparisons span evaluation instances rather than necessarily repeated calls for one fixed instance, so interpretation as local stability needs caution; Q6 single case study; Q8 no code link found; Q9 clinical data, ethics brief; Q10 30 runs.','Publisher Explanation stability section; preserve original Q5=0.5 pending methodological review.')
add('S78','limitations','Authors: single-institution MIMIC-IV data without external validation; structured first-24-hour EHR variables only; quantitative proxies and expert ratings without prospective clinical decision evaluation (pp.10–11). Ours: internally inconsistent Anchors AOPC and run-variance summaries (p.10); no identifiable code URL despite repository claims; repeated-model-run protocol not established.','Local N480.txt pp.10–11 author limitations; p.10 Table6 gives Anchors AOPC .239 vs .148 in Table10/prose, and CV best/worst ordering conflicts with Table8.')
add('S76','findings','NDT-LIME improved fidelity on most benchmarks while trading some repeated-run stability for expressiveness; input-neighbor regularity was evaluated separately (Secs.3–4, Table 2).','Local N557.txt pp.11–13 distinguishes algorithmic repeated-call variability, regularity and fidelity; Table2 shows nonuniform tradeoffs.','clarification')
(root/'work/audit_saif/proposed_patches.json').write_text(json.dumps(patches,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Audit:',root/'work/audit_saif.md')
print('Proposed patches:',len(patches))
